				<r3d:repositoryUrl>http://ifri.forgov.org/</r3d:repositoryUrl>
				<r3d:description language="eng">The IFRI research network examines how governance arrangements affect forests and the people who depend on them. It is comprised of 14 Collaborating Research Centers located around the globe. Researchers use a common data collection method to ensure that sites can be compared across space and time. The IFRI database contains information about biodiversity, livelihoods, institutions, and forest carbon for over 250 sites in 15 countries between 1992 and the present.</r3d:description>
